</section>

<section id="view-roadmap" class="view" hidden>
  <p class="intro">The road to the platinum, in the order this guide recommends. Each stage lists the trophies it covers and the counts the official descriptions give — 4 chapters, 8 stranger strands, 250 stunts, 42 Shooting Range challenges, 100 WAiNK It locations, 100 vehicles, 3 card sets, 5 bank vaults, 50 challenges.</p>
  <ol class="roadmap" id="roadmap"></ol>
</section>

<section id="view-about" class="view" hidden>
  <h2>How this guide was made</h2>
  <p>Every trophy's <strong>name, description and grade</strong> is shown exactly as PlayStation publishes it, as listed by Exophase and PSNProfiles before this guide was written. Every <strong>guide</strong> is written in this guide's own words. Where a guide gives a specific location or step, it says where the fact comes from; where no source publishes the detail — for example the number of meditation spots, or what exactly triggers “Personal Best” — the guide says so instead of inventing one. A cited guide beats an uncited one, however detailed.</p>
  <h2>How to use the tracker</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Tick a trophy when you earn it. Ticks are saved in this browser (localStorage) and survive reloads.</li>
    <li><strong>Export progress</strong> downloads a small JSON file; <strong>Import progress</strong> loads one back. Keep the export as a backup before clearing browser data.</li>
    <li><strong>Hide story spoilers</strong> replaces the names and descriptions of story trophies you have not earned yet with a hidden placeholder. Earned trophies always show.</li>
    <li><strong>Missable</strong> flags the three trophies tied to a one-time moment: two story choices and one stealth attempt. Save before story choices.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Offline</h2>
  <p>This guide is plain static files. It loads nothing from the network, uses no external fonts or images, and works with the network off.</p>
  <p class="fineprint">An unofficial fan guide. Grand Theft Auto, GTA and Rockstar Games are trademarks of their owners; this guide uses no Rockstar logo, artwork, box art or game screenshots.</p>
</section>

<footer>
  <p>Leonida Trophy Guide — an unofficial offline guide for GTA VI on PS5. Names, descriptions and grades are PlayStation's official list; guides are this site's own words, with sources named beside each one.</p>
</footer>
<script type="module" src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
